Z||000003||mrfiero||12-30-2001||09:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cyberkhat:<BR><B>Question Neal: What is that gauge mounted in the engine bay? </B><P>Looks like a fuel pressure gauge to me.<P><B> I got a blue 87 GT too and want to drop a 3.4 in it.I just wish I could hurry up and blow up the 2.8 in it a little faster - its only got 53,000 on it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You don't necessarily need to have a blown engine to put in a 3.4.  Build up the 3.4 then sell the stock 2.8 to offset things.<P>If you must blow your original engine first, just drain most or all of the oil then drive it hard......she'll be knocking in no time!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
